      "text": "To find the new class mean after the additional six students took the test, we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the total score of the initial 30 students:**\n   Given that the mean score of the initial 30 students is \\(72\\%\\), we use the formula for the mean:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total score of the initial 30 students} = \\text{mean} \\times \\text{number of students}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total score} = 72\\% \\times 30 = 2160\\%\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the total score of the additional six students:**\n   The mean score of the additional six students is \\(78\\%\\). Therefore, the total score for these six students is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total score of the additional six students} = 78\\% \\times 6 = 468\\%\n   \\]\n\n3. **Sum the total scores of both groups:**\n   Add the total scores from both groups to find the combined total score:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Combined total score} = 2160\\% + 468\\% = 2628\\%\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the total number of students:**\n   Initially, there were 30 students. After the additional six students took the test, the total number of students is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total number of students} = 30 + 6 = 36\n   \\]\n\n5. **Find the new class mean:**\n   To find the new class mean, divide the combined total score by the total number of students:\n   \\[\n   \\text{New class mean} = \\frac{\\text{Combined total score}}{\\text{Total number of students}} = \\frac{2628\\%}{36}\n   \\]\n\n6. **Perform the division:**\n   \\[\n   \\frac{2628\\%}{36} = 73\\%\n   \\]\n\nThus, the new class mean after the additional six students took the test is \\(\\boxed{73\\%}\\).",
