      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the new class mean, we need to calculate the total score on the test and then divide by the total number of students.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the total score for the 30 students who took the test on the first day. The mean score of these 30 students is 72%, so the total score for these 30 students is:\n\\[ 30 \\times 72 = 2160 \\]\n\nNext, let's calculate the total score for the 6 students who took the test on the second day. The mean score of these 6 students is 78%, so the total score for these 6 students is:\n\\[ 6 \\times 78 = 468 \\]\n\nNow, we can find the total score for all 36 students by adding the total scores of the two groups of students:\n\\[ 2160 + 468 = 2628 \\]\n\nFinally, we calculate the new class mean by dividing the total score by the total number of students:\n\\[ \\frac{2628}{36} = 73 \\]\n\nTherefore, the new class mean is \\(\\boxed{73}\\).",
