      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the new class mean after including the scores of the remaining six students, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total score of the first 30 students.\n2. Calculate the total score of the remaining 6 students.\n3. Calculate the new total score for the entire class.\n4. Find the new class mean by dividing the new total score by the total number of students (36).\n\nLet's start with the first step:\n\n1. Calculate the total score of the first 30 students.\n   The mean score of the first 30 students is 72%. Therefore, the total score of these 30 students is:\n   \\[\n   30 \\times 72 = 2160\n   \\]\n\n2. Calculate the total score of the remaining 6 students.\n   The mean score of the remaining 6 students is 78%. Therefore, the total score of these 6 students is:\n   \\[\n   6 \\times 78 = 468\n   \\]\n\n3. Calculate the new total score for the entire class.\n   The new total score is the sum of the total scores of the first 30 students and the remaining 6 students:\n   \\[\n   2160 + 468 = 2628\n   \\]\n\n4. Find the new class mean by dividing the new total score by the total number of students (36):\n   \\[\n   \\frac{2628}{36} = 73\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the new class mean is \\(\\boxed{73}\\).",
